  "query_preview": "..\n(Monday through Thursday)\nIssued at 122 AM CST Fri Nov 20 2026\n\nUpper flow transitioning more zonal on Monday but becoming \nsouthwesterly by Tuesday with the approach of another wave coming \nthrough for mid-week.  No surface front with this upper system but \nwill bring a reinforcing surge of much colder air coming down from \nthe north on Tuesday with areas west and north of the I-44 corridor \nnot warming out of the 40s.  We do have the potential for hard \nfreezes early next week especially on Tuesday night/Wednesday \nmorning down into central Oklahoma as the reinforcing colder air \ncomes through with low temperatures well in the 20s.  As far as \nprecipitation with early next weeks system, there is a 15-20% chance \nfor brief light snow to light rain/snow mix across far northwestern \nOklahoma on Tuesday morning with little to no accumulations or \nimpacts.",
